From: "Mattias Engdegård" <f91-men@nada.kth.se>
Date: Sat, 2 Sep 2000 22:50:58 +0200 (MET DST)
Version: 0.6

It's often hard to enter tunnels on the Solaris version of Heroes --- the
player is bounced away as if it was an obstacle. And sometimes the player
can enter the tunnel but is shifted sideways, and it looks strange.
I've put some screenshots at ftp://ptah.lnf.kth.se/pub/misc/hbug[0-2].png

I suspect that the endianness might have something to do with it, or maybe
the use of an uninitialised variable somewhere.

----------

From: "Mattias Engdegård" <f91-men@nada.kth.se>
Date: Mon, 4 Sep 2000 22:10:50 +0200 (MET DST)
Version: 0.6

>>Just to narrow my search: does tunnels always behave identicaly?
>>E.g. is the bug of hbug1.png persistant across different runs of
>>the game?  Or can the same tunnel behave differently in the same
>>conditions?

Yes, it seems to behave randomly. It always deflects the vehicle and forces
a 90-degree turn, but sometimes the vehicle manages to pass through anyway
(essentially variations of hbug1.png - sometimes even more bizarre).

>>Does the problem only occur when you take a tunnel from right
>>to left?

No, it occurs from both directions.

>>On one tunnel tile (the blocks used to build the level) there is
>>usually two tunnel-entry squares (squares are the size of the
>>vehicle, there is 4 squares per tile), have you noticed if
>>*both* entries for the same tile were not working or if only one
>>wasn't and the other worked fine?

No, there seems to be no such difference.

